	That's not really the case. There's some overlap between the
sets, but they're definitely distinct. #offering *any* deceased pet will
get you in trouble (though I'm not sure about ex-pets that went feral
before their deaths). Eating deceased pets is fine, though, as long as
they're not cats, dogs, or your own species. You can #offer non-pet cats
and dogs with no problem, but eating them will get you in trouble.
Eating co-aligned unicorns is fine, but #offering them isn't, nor is
killing them. (#offering unicorns that are co-aligned with the *altar*
(while we're on the subject of converting them) is also a Bad Idea.)
Eating or #offering your own species is a problem.

	And if you're chaotic, orcish, and/or a caveperson, various
parts of these rules are suspended. Chaotics can #offer their own
species without seriously bad effects; orcs and cavepeople aren't
restricted from cannibalism or eating cats and dogs. But even chaotic
orcs get in trouble for #offering former pets or co-aligned unicorns.

